Author: Danny Milosavljevic <dannym@friendly-machines.com>
Date: 2026-04-20
Subject: Mirror NOTARGETWIN32 guard around the second winstackpagesize site
License: expat

`compiler/i386/cga.pas' brings `t_win32' into its uses clause only
when win32 target support is enabled:

    {$ifndef NOTARGETWIN32}
           ,t_win32
    {$endif}

and `winstackpagesize' is declared in t_win32 (it's just `4096'
there).

cga.pas references `winstackpagesize' at two sites.  The first,
the `getmem' growing-array stack-touch loop) is correctly
wrapped in `{$ifndef NOTARGETWIN32}'.  The second (the
stack-frame setup in `genentrycode') is not -- it just
runtime-guards on `target_os.id=os_i386_win32'.
Compiling with `-dNOTARGETWIN32' therefore drops `t_win32' from
the uses clause and the unguarded site fails to resolve
`winstackpagesize' at parse time.

Wrap the second site's win32 arm (condition + body) in the same
`{$ifndef NOTARGETWIN32}' block.

--- a/compiler/i386/cga.pas
+++ b/compiler/i386/cga.pas
@@ -3597,6 +3597,7 @@
               if stackframe<>0 then
                   begin
                           begin
+{$ifndef NOTARGETWIN32}
                             { windows guards only a few pages for stack growing, }
                             { so we have to access every page first              }
                             if (target_os.id=os_i386_win32) and
@@ -3638,6 +3639,7 @@
                                     end
                               end
                             else
+{$endif NOTARGETWIN32}
                               exprasmlist^.insert(new(paicpu,op_const_reg(A_SUB,S_L,stackframe,R_ESP)));
                             if (cs_check_stack in aktlocalswitches) and
                               not(target_info.target in [target_i386_freebsd,target_i386_netbsd,
